#Problem APEX 4.1.10

## DBsubject(Calculus - single variable)
## DBchapter(Applications of differentiation)
## DBsection(Newton's method)
## KEYWORDS("Newton's method", 'rootfinding')
## Institution(Valdosta State University)
## Author(S. V. Ault)
## MLT(Newton-f-value-graph)
## Level(2)
## MO(1)
## TitleText1('APEX Calculus')
## AuthorText1('Hartman')
## EditionText1('3.0')
## Section1('4.1')
## Problem1('10')

DOCUMENT();

loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'plots.pl',  'PGcourse.pl');
Context('Numeric')->flags->set(    tolerance => 0.0001,    tolType   => "absolute");

$a1 = random(5, 10);

$f  = Formula("x^17 - 2x^13 - 10x^8 + $a1");
$df = $f->D('x');

$fx = "x^{17} - 2x^{13} - 10x^8 + $a1";

@xa = (-1);
for my $k (0..4) { push(@xa, $xa[$k] - $f->eval(x => $xa[$k])/$df->eval(x=>$xa[$k]));}

@xb = (1);
for my $k (0..4) { push(@xb, $xb[$k] - $f->eval(x => $xb[$k])/$df->eval(x=>$xb[$k]));}

@xc = (1.5);
for my $k (0..4) { push(@xc, $xc[$k] - $f->eval(x => $xc[$k])/$df->eval(x=>$xc[$k]));}


$ans = List($xa[-1], $xb[-1], $xc[-1]);

$plot = Plot(xmin => -2, xmax => 2, xtick_delta => 1, xminor => 0,
            ymin => -10, ymax => 10, ytick_delta => 5, yminor => 4, rounded_corners => 1);
$plot->add_function($f,'x', -2,2,color => 'blue');

$altText =
    "A function that rises through an intercept near x=-1, hits "
    . "a maximum near x=0, then falls through an intercept near x=1, "
    . " hits a minimum, then rises through an intercept near x=1.5.";

BEGIN_PGML
Use Newton's Method to approximate all roots of the given
function, within the given interval,
accurate to 4 places after the decimal.  Use
the graph below to obtain good initial approximations.
[```  
   f(x) = [$fx], \quad \textrm{on} \; (-2, 2)
```] 

>> [![$altText]!]{$plot}{$w} <<


Root(s): [_]{$ans}{30}

(Separate multiple answers by commas.)
END_PGML

###################################

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
Set up the iterative formula for Newton's Method:
[```
  x_{n+1} = x_n - \dfrac{f(x_n)}{f'(x_n)} 
  = x_n - \dfrac{x_n^{17} - 2x_n^{13} - 10x_n^8 + [$a1]}{17x_n^{16} - 26x_n^{12} - 80x_n^7}
```]

There are three roots.  The smallest is near [`x = [$xa[0]]`].
Using Newton's Method,
[```
  \begin{aligned}
    x_0 &= [$xa[0]] \\
    x_1 &\approx [$xa[1]] \\
    x_2 &\approx [$xa[2]] \\
    x_3 &\approx [$xa[3]] \\
    x_4 &\approx [$xa[4]] \\
    x_5 &\approx [$xa[5]]
  \end{aligned}
```]

The next root is near [`x = [$xb[0]]`].
Using Newton's Method,
[```
  \begin{aligned}
    x_0 &= [$xb[0]] \\
    x_1 &\approx [$xb[1]] \\
    x_2 &\approx [$xb[2]] \\
    x_3 &\approx [$xb[3]] \\
    x_4 &\approx [$xb[4]] \\
    x_5 &\approx [$xb[5]]
  \end{aligned}
```]

The largest root is near [`x = [$xc[0]]`].
Using Newton's Method,
[```
  \begin{aligned}
    x_0 &= [$xc[0]] \\
    x_1 &\approx [$xc[1]] \\
    x_2 &\approx [$xc[2]] \\
    x_3 &\approx [$xc[3]] \\
    x_4 &\approx [$xc[4]] \\
    x_5 &\approx [$xc[5]] 
  \end{aligned}
```]
END_PGML_SOLUTION
ENDDOCUMENT();

